anika: Quick heads-up  I'm opening a small docs PR to converge the SDK streaming + pagination + retries snippets across py/ts/go. Found subtle differences that confuse customers (resume tokens vs ids, partial-json chunk handling). PR when ready.

peter: Awesome. One ask: make the pagination examples use an opaque `cursor` name everywhere and include a short note: 'do not parse'. Lots of customers tried to decode it into offsets.

lucas: Agree. Also, let's show a tiny resume pattern for streaming: keep the last chunk id and pass it as `resume_from` if reconnecting. Keep it optional in the snippet.

tess: For TS please show both `for await` and `ReadableStream.getReader()` usage. Also include a 2-line accumulate+parse example for partial JSON chunks.

anika: Plan: Python -> async generator with resume token + reconnect-on-transient example. TS -> iterator + reader + chunk accumulation + retry helper. Go -> SSE-like loop with bufio.Scanner + minimal backoff helper. Also a short migration note about cursor naming and backport checklist for legacy quickstarts.

peter: I prefer the docs include a tiny retry helper instead of suggesting customers import libs. Keep it copy-pasteable, non-opinionated. Example suggestion for TS: 

```ts
async function retry<T>(fn: ()=>Promise<T>, attempts=3){
  for(let i=0;i<attempts;i++){
    try { return await fn() }
    catch(e){ if(i===attempts-1) throw e; await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r, 100*(i+1))) }
  }
}
```

lucas: For Python streaming snippet: 

```py
last_id = None
async for part in client.chat.stream(prompt, resume_from=last_id):
    print(part.text)
    if hasattr(part, 'id'):
        last_id = part.id
# on transient: reconnect and pass resume_from=last_id
```

tess: TS chunk accumulation example: 

```ts
let buf = ''
for await (const c of client.chat.stream({model, input})){
  buf += c.text
  try { const obj = JSON.parse(buf); handle(obj); buf = '' } catch(e) { /* wait for more */ }
}
```

anika: Go sample will show a scanner loop and a tiny backoff util: 

```go
func tryDo(attempts int, fn func() error) error {
  for i:=0;i<attempts;i++{
    if err:=fn(); err!=nil { time.Sleep(time.Millisecond*100*time.Duration(i+1)); continue }
    return nil
  }
  return fmt.Errorf("failed after retries")
}

scanner := bufio.NewScanner(resp.Body)
for scanner.Scan() { handle(scanner.Text()) }
```

peter: Great. Also add a short "If items missing after migration" troubleshooting note: likely eventual consistency with edge caches; recommend a short re-fetch window (e.g., re-query last 5m) or a backfill using timestamps.

lucas: One more: call out multipart streaming / rerank flows where each chunk may contain metadata + token text. Show how to check `chunk.type` and update resume id only after persisting metadata.

anika: Will do. I'll open the PR and request reviews from @peter and @tess. Draft will include a backport checklist for archived quickstarts (v0.7/v0.8) and a migration blurb listing legacy aliases (`page_token`, `cursor_token`).

